{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1228609-second-time-creating-a-new-spell-what-do-you-think","id":1228609,"title":"Second Time Creating a New SPell: What Do You Think?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-06-19T09:52:27-07:00","id":1228609,"title":"Second Time Creating a New SPell: What Do You Think?","content":"Thousand Year Horror<br /> Cost: 20sm, 1wp (25sm, 2wp, 1a)<br /> Duration: One Scene<br /> Keywords: Perilous<br /> <br /> The sorcerer reaches into the annals of history, drawing forth a truly horrific beast of myth and legend. Those on the battlefield find they have a hard time facing against such a mighty and terrifying foe.<br /> <br /> After casting Thousand Year Horror, any Battle Groups up to Long range must make an immediate rout check at a -1 penalty. If they succeed, they take a penalty to their Defense equal to the caster's Essence. Additionally, the caster can then use their turn to command the beast to attack. Any initiative stolen from an opponent is added to the sorcerer's initiative total. Any damage done to the beast is instead inflicted upon the caster. The Horror has the following statistics:<br /> <br /> Claw: Close, 8 dice (8 damage, minimum 2)<br /> Tail: Short, 6 dice (11 damage, minimum 4)<br /> <br /> If the caster pays the cost in parentheses instead of the normal cost, the Horror gains +2 dice to each attack option, and the range band for each extends by one. Additionally, the rout check is made at a -3, and the Defense penalty is (Essence+1).<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Co-Host of <a href=\"http://www.fivepoles.com/podcast\" target=\"_blank\">The Deliberative Podcast</a><br /> Follow us on <a href=\"http://www.twitter.com/deliberativepod\" target=\"_blank\">Twitter</a>!<br /> Follow us on <a href=\"http://www.facebook.com/thedeliberativepodcast\" target=\"_blank\">Facebook</a>!<br /> Follow us on the <a href=\"http://www.fivepoles.com\" target=\"_blank\">Web</a>!<br /> Like what we do? Support us on <a href=\"http://patreon.com/thedeliberative\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4164-lukkychukky","name":"Lukkychukky","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4164_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"126"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-19T12:16:15-07:00","id":1228641,"title":"","content":"Interesting idea. Hard to make a productive comment if we don't know what Circle the spell is? If its meant to be Celestial, then this currently looks like a poor choice compared to Magma Kraken? The Kraken attacks and takes damage independantly, and attacks as an artefact wielded using whats likely to be my best stats (Int+Occult).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6230-katana1515","name":"Katana1515","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6230_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"280"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-19T12:44:17-07:00","id":1228650,"title":"","content":"I'd say it's probably too weak to be practical to use even as a Terrestrial spell. Its only use seems to be fighting battle groups - but you already have Death of Obsidian Butterflies for that, and you even get initiative for using it (whereas this thing just chases them away <i>very slowly</i>).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=943303#post943303\" target=\"_blank\">Evocations for the demonic tattoos gained from the Pact with Mara sorcerous initiation</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=907071#post907071\" target=\"_blank\">Pyre-Kindler (Soulsteel and Red Jade Grimscythe, Artifact 3)</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1072019-soulsteel-stormcaller-concept-gravedigger?p=1074897#post1074897\" target=\"_blank\">Tenebrous Descent (Stormcaller's Black Jade Reaver Daiklave cousin, Artifact 5)</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1074256-combat-with-corebook-shikari-antagonists?p=1074303#post1074303\" target=\"_blank\">Advice for running the corebook shikari antagonists</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3443-aluminiumtrioxid","name":"aluminiumtrioxid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3443_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-19T14:54:29-07:00","id":1228685,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>aluminiumtrioxid</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1228609-second-time-creating-a-new-spell-what-do-you-think?p=1228650#post1228650\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd say it's probably too weak to be practical to use even as a Terrestrial spell. Its only use seems to be fighting battle groups - but you already have Death of Obsidian Butterflies for that, and you even get initiative for using it (whereas this thing just chases them away <i>very slowly</i>).</div> </div> </div> </div>Well it doesn't HAVE to fight a Battlegroup. It talks about steeling initiative, which doesn't happen against BGs, so it seems to have rules for both scenarios.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I post Artifacts in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>. How I make them is in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/828820-how-to-write-artifacts-and-evocations\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>.<br /> I have made many tools and other things for 3rd Edition. I now host all of my creations on my Google site: <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/unsungherovault/home\" target=\"_blank\">The Vault of the Unsung Hero</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/368-the-unsung-hero","name":"The Unsung Hero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar368_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2288"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-19T21:09:05-07:00","id":1228749,"title":"","content":"Does this horror from history try to shake off my yoke of command? If I am struck down, does the beast disappear? Can someone try to win the beast away from me? What defenses does the beast have? What is it's STR and Athletics? Is it Legendary Sized? <br /> <br /> And I might just be dense, but what does the 1a cost mean?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Please be warned: this is not champagne, this is most likely a duck.<br /> -<i>Chausse</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\"><i>Message me for Japanese translations.</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8830-sorcerous-overlord","name":"Sorcerous Overlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8830_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-20T07:02:44-07:00","id":1228844,"title":"","content":"Wow. All good insights and questions. This is meant to be Terrestrial Circle. 1a means one anima level. As far as <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8830-sorcerous-overlord\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar8830_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"8830\" data-vbnamecard=\"8830\">Sorcerous Overlord</a>'s questions, no, you have complete control. It's like an extremely real illusion, I think? If you die, the beast disappears. I hadn't considered Defenses, TBH. i know the numbers need some work. I just wanted to create a spell that wasn't DoOB, and was a bit more aspected to fighting BG's. Also, DoOB fires and is gone. i wanted something to stick around. Any other changes or reqorks would be greatly appreciated.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Co-Host of <a href=\"http://www.fivepoles.com/podcast\" target=\"_blank\">The Deliberative Podcast</a><br /> Follow us on <a href=\"http://www.twitter.com/deliberativepod\" target=\"_blank\">Twitter</a>!<br /> Follow us on <a href=\"http://www.facebook.com/thedeliberativepodcast\" target=\"_blank\">Facebook</a>!<br /> Follow us on the <a href=\"http://www.fivepoles.com\" target=\"_blank\">Web</a>!<br /> Like what we do? Support us on <a href=\"http://patreon.com/thedeliberative\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4164-lukkychukky","name":"Lukkychukky","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4164_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"126"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-20T19:52:00-07:00","id":1229049,"title":"","content":"Wait. Thousand year horror is a... terrestrial spell?<br /> <br /> With that name, I was hoping for celestial or solar.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-22T10:29:23-07:00","id":1229392,"title":"","content":"Hmmm perhaps it would help to define the intent of the spell more first? Are you summoning a distinct entity, a potent phantasm, or using sorcery to give yourself a couple of extra animalistic limbs to attack with (kind of like a Lovecraftian version of Doctor Octopus)? Each of these strikes me as good fodder for a terrestrial spell, but at the moment your fluff text implies the former and the mechanics seem to lean towards the latter (with the fact it uses your actions and initiative.) If you firm up exactly what the spell is intended to do, then perhaps we can make more useful suggestions regarding mechanics to fit that image?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6230-katana1515","name":"Katana1515","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6230_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"280"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-22T10:34:38-07:00","id":1229395,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12952\" data-vbnamecard=\"12952\">Accelerator</a>, it was designed for use by one of the players in my group who only knows terrestrial sorcery. I just arbitrarily came up with the name. <br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6230-katana1515\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar6230_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"6230\" data-vbnamecard=\"6230\">Katana1515</a>, the idea was to have a spell which would be effective against battle groups, but would also give some measure of melee combat ability for the scene. I view it more as a very realistic phantom, since damage to it affects the caster. So, to clear up...<br /> <br /> I want a spell with the primary purpose of forcing routs in battle groups, but then giving some c on at ability to the caster which would last for a scene. That\u2019s the kernel of the idea.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Co-Host of <a href=\"http://www.fivepoles.com/podcast\" target=\"_blank\">The Deliberative Podcast</a><br /> Follow us on <a href=\"http://www.twitter.com/deliberativepod\" target=\"_blank\">Twitter</a>!<br /> Follow us on <a href=\"http://www.facebook.com/thedeliberativepodcast\" target=\"_blank\">Facebook</a>!<br /> Follow us on the <a href=\"http://www.fivepoles.com\" target=\"_blank\">Web</a>!<br /> Like what we do? Support us on <a href=\"http://patreon.com/thedeliberative\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4164-lukkychukky","name":"Lukkychukky","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4164_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"126"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-22T15:17:47-07:00","id":1229466,"title":"","content":"Frankly, I read this spell and wonder why I\u2019d ever not learn Butterflies and Claws instead even if that\u2019s two spells versus one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-28T06:59:24-07:00","id":1230801,"title":"","content":"Fair point. My thinking was that DoOB is a short spell, blast and done. I wanted something which would stick around, like Wood Claws. But Wood Claws doesn't have anything effect like DoOB. So, this new one has a mass effect and then also gives some combat ability for the duration of the encounter. Seems like a solid idea to me. But I'm sure it could be balanced better.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Co-Host of <a href=\"http://www.fivepoles.com/podcast\" target=\"_blank\">The Deliberative Podcast</a><br /> Follow us on <a href=\"http://www.twitter.com/deliberativepod\" target=\"_blank\">Twitter</a>!<br /> Follow us on <a href=\"http://www.facebook.com/thedeliberativepodcast\" target=\"_blank\">Facebook</a>!<br /> Follow us on the <a href=\"http://www.fivepoles.com\" target=\"_blank\">Web</a>!<br /> Like what we do? Support us on <a href=\"http://patreon.com/thedeliberative\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4164-lukkychukky","name":"Lukkychukky","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4164_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"126"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-28T08:13:59-07:00","id":1230822,"title":"","content":"So the idea sounds fun. A big freaky image to rout enemies (maybe adds to intimidate like Dawn Caste anima does but not as strongly?), and gives you a melee &amp; thrown ranged attack (thats what i consider short range distance attacks).<br /> Maybe it could be more or less solid and thats changes some effects, more illusory makes it focus on scaring, adding anima gives it substance to do more physical things like damage<br /> <br /> Edit add: if someone twists your spell from you, the fear strikes yourself and you suffer the fear penalties too!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24220,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24220-cryo-seraph","user":"Cryo-Seraph","date":". 06-28-2018, 11:20 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24220-cryo-seraph","name":"Cryo-Seraph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24220_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"72"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-28T10:15:29-07:00","id":1230850,"title":"","content":"Yeah, that's the basic gist of it. I like the idea of the distort effect! I LOVE the idea of raising your anima to give it more substance!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Co-Host of <a href=\"http://www.fivepoles.com/podcast\" target=\"_blank\">The Deliberative Podcast</a><br /> Follow us on <a href=\"http://www.twitter.com/deliberativepod\" target=\"_blank\">Twitter</a>!<br /> Follow us on <a href=\"http://www.facebook.com/thedeliberativepodcast\" target=\"_blank\">Facebook</a>!<br /> Follow us on the <a href=\"http://www.fivepoles.com\" target=\"_blank\">Web</a>!<br /> Like what we do? Support us on <a href=\"http://patreon.com/thedeliberative\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4164-lukkychukky","name":"Lukkychukky","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4164_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"126"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-28T13:36:25-07:00","id":1230913,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lukkychukky</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1228609-second-time-creating-a-new-spell-what-do-you-think?p=1230801#post1230801\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Fair point. My thinking was that DoOB is a short spell, blast and done. I wanted something which would stick around, like Wood Claws. But Wood Claws doesn't have anything effect like DoOB. So, this new one has a mass effect and then also gives some combat ability for the duration of the encounter. Seems like a solid idea to me. But I'm sure it could be balanced better.</div> </div> </div> </div>The problem is, not only is this spell significantly worse as an anti-battle group tool than DoOB and significantly worse as a combat buff than WDC, but those two use cases are largely mutually-exclusive in the first place in terms of what I'd actually want to do in a given fight. If I'm fighting a battle group and I know DoOB I'm not going to bother with WDC because DoOB is tailor-made to curbstomp battle groups so any turn I spend attacking with WDC is probably one I'd be better off using to shape DoOB.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-28T16:20:14-07:00","id":1230940,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sith_Happens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1228609-second-time-creating-a-new-spell-what-do-you-think?p=1230913#post1230913\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The problem is, not only is this spell significantly worse as an anti-battle group tool than DoOB and significantly worse as a combat buff than WDC, but those two use cases are largely mutually-exclusive in the first place in terms of what I'd actually want to do in a given fight. If I'm fighting a battle group and I know DoOB I'm not going to bother with WDC because DoOB is tailor-made to curbstomp battle groups so <b>any turn I spend attacking with WDC is probably one I'd be better off using to shape DoOB.</b></div> </div> </div> </div>Hardly. Death of Obsidian Butterflies is great against battle groups, but you still need a half-decent pile of Initiative for it to be truly effective. Sure, you might really luck out on your Join Battle roll, but having an effective Artifact weapon with which to launch a Withering attack or two can help out significantly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-29T04:38:56-07:00","id":1231069,"title":"","content":"All valid points. So, if you wanted to create a spell designed to be used against BG's, and one that isn't DoOB, what kind of spell would you look at making? Terrestrial circle, mind you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Co-Host of <a href=\"http://www.fivepoles.com/podcast\" target=\"_blank\">The Deliberative Podcast</a><br /> Follow us on <a href=\"http://www.twitter.com/deliberativepod\" target=\"_blank\">Twitter</a>!<br /> Follow us on <a href=\"http://www.facebook.com/thedeliberativepodcast\" target=\"_blank\">Facebook</a>!<br /> Follow us on the <a href=\"http://www.fivepoles.com\" target=\"_blank\">Web</a>!<br /> Like what we do? Support us on <a href=\"http://patreon.com/thedeliberative\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4164-lukkychukky","name":"Lukkychukky","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4164_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"126"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-29T15:32:41-07:00","id":1231231,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1228609-second-time-creating-a-new-spell-what-do-you-think?p=1230940#post1230940\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hardly. Death of Obsidian Butterflies is great against battle groups, but you still need a half-decent pile of Initiative for it to be truly effective. Sure, you might really luck out on your Join Battle roll, but having an effective Artifact weapon with which to launch a Withering attack or two can help out significantly.</div> </div> </div> </div>Obsidian Butterflies doesn't use your initiative, you're probably getting it mixed up with Brilliant Raptor.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lukkychukky</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1228609-second-time-creating-a-new-spell-what-do-you-think?p=1231069#post1231069\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">All valid points. So, if you wanted to create a spell designed to be used against BG's, and one that isn't DoOB, what kind of spell would you look at making? Terrestrial circle, mind you.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think you're on the right track with the fear-inducing angle, which isn't something explored yet by a published Terrestrial spell, so I'd make that what it revolves around.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}